name: keep-pilot-and-rubric-out-of-solution
description: "In car-insurance, solution artifacts (flow criteria, constitution, ADRs, specs) must speak only about the product problem, never the job-test rubric or the Roclec pilot"
metadata:
  node_type: memory
  type: feedback
  originSessionId: f9ebb916-7034-4417-9bcc-3122c3729747
  modified: 2026-11-23T05:47:19.107Z
---

Solution artifacts in car-insurance (flow.toml criteria, constitution, ADRs, specs, skills) must be grounded only in the product problem: the multi-country wizard, `docs/assessment/02-context-and-functional-scope.md` and `docs/assessment/04-user-stories.md`. Do not reference the assessment's grading rubric (`07-evaluation-criteria.md`, score percentages), deliverable rules, or the Roclec pilot inside them, and do not justify proposals by "it scores X %".

**Why:** the user said the assessment is a job test and the Roclec pilot is a separate concern; mixing them pollutes the solution the reviewers read.

**How to apply:** when proposing wording or justifications, cite the business context, functional scope, user stories or engineering reasons. The pilot lives only in `docs/pilot/bitacora.md`. See [[roclec-pilot-workflow]].

